cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it as below. This is coursework research code;
  it is not a peer-reviewed publication. Please also cite the original algorithms you use,
  in particular AAA (Nakatsukasa, Sete & Trefethen 2018).
type: software
title: "Quantum Scattering Surrogates: surrogate modeling and adaptive sampling for 1D quantum resonance reconstruction"
version: 0.1.0
authors:
  # TODO(author): replace the alias with your full name (given-names / family-names) before publishing
  - alias: Apostal322
repository-code: "https://github.com/Apostal322/kurca4"
abstract: >-
  Reproducible research code comparing classical interpolation, Gaussian processes,
  AAA rational approximation and PyTorch neural-network surrogates, with and without
  adaptive sampling, for reconstructing energy- and parameter-dependent transmission
  amplitudes of one-dimensional quantum scattering with narrow resonances, under equal
  budgets of exact solver evaluations.
keywords:
  - quantum scattering
  - surrogate modeling
  - rational approximation
  - adaptive sampling
  - pytorch
  - computational physics
references:
  - type: article
    authors:
      - family-names: Nakatsukasa
        given-names: Yuji
      - family-names: Sète
        given-names: Olivier
      - family-names: Trefethen
        given-names: Lloyd N.
    title: "The AAA algorithm for rational approximation"
    journal: "SIAM Journal on Scientific Computing"
    volume: 40
    issue: 3
    start: A1494
    end: A1522
    year: 2018
